window.products.push({"id":278960,"name":"Victorinox-Swiss-Army-Cutlery Rosewood Santoku Knife, Granton Blade, 7-Inch","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":55.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/5143uMmeoVL._AC_SL1200_.jpg","description":"A TRUSTED FAVORITE An elegant addition to any kitchen, the 7\" Victorinox Rosewood Santoku Knife can handle nearly every kitchen task imaginable. Crafted with a comfortable handle, superior weight and balance, and a razor sharp Granton blade that rarely requires re-sharpening, this knife is an essential tool for every kitchen. KEY FEATURES High-quality, lightweight European steel. High-quality, lightweight European steel. Handle design reduces hand and wrist fatigue. Handle design reduces hand and wrist fatigue. Santoku blade fit for slicing, dicing, and mincing. Santoku blade fit for slicing, dicing, and mincing. Granton blade that minimizes friction & prevents food from sticking. Granton blade that minimizes friction & prevents food from sticking. Flat spine for extra power to slice through hard-skinned items. Flat spine for extra power to slice through hard-skinned items. Hand polished rosewood handle for a secure and comfortable grip no matter the hand size. Hand polished rosewood handle for a secure and comfortable grip no matter the hand size. Dishwasher safe & easy to sharpen. Dishwasher safe & easy to sharpen. CARE AND USE Be good to your knives and they’ll be good to you. Following these simple guidelines will ensure that you get the longest life out of your knife! CLEANING Victorinox Swiss Army recommends washing all knives by hand. For best results, hand wash your knives with a soapy cloth and dry immediately.  While Fibrox Pro knives are dishwasher safe, we recommend hand washing as dishwashers are designed to spray water at a relatively high pressure, which can jostle the silverware and cause the knives to collide, dulling the edge. SHARPENING For optimum performance, knives should be honed after every couple of uses. Proper and frequent use of a honing steel will keep your knives sharper and performing at their best. FORMERLY FORSCHNER In 1937 Victorinox began selling cutlery in America through a Connecticut distributor called R.H. Forschner & Co. A well-known manufacturer of butcher scales, Forschner soon became the exclusive U.S. distributor for Victorinox knives, and was the name by which Victorinox knives were known.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/5143uMmeoVL._AC_SL1200_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Victorinox","source_asin":"B01M7QA0X9","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-278960","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B01M7QA0X9","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B01M7QA0X9","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
